    "created_at": "2016-09-15T05:32:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-15T05:32:42Z",
    "body": "`ping` is the only attribute that Gecko reflects as a space-separated list of URLs, yes.  Looks like we've done that ever since initial implementation in 2006.\n\nI don't have any particular strong feelings about keeping that behavior, or just returning the underlying attr value.  What do other UAs do?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
